---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Terms of Use" description="Terms for using Integrated Math resources, accounts, and competition services.">
  <article class="site-container policy-page">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="privacy-note">Last updated October 17, 2026.</p>
    <p>These terms cover the Integrated Math website, its learning resources, and its contest services. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@integratedmath.org">info@integratedmath.org</a>.</p>
    <h2>Competitions</h2>
    <p>Each competition has its own rules, deadlines, eligibility requirements, permitted tools, and submission instructions. Read the relevant <a href="/competitions">competition page</a> and portal instructions before starting. Those instructions govern the event, including grading, security review, and disqualification.</p>
    <h2>Accounts and responsible use</h2>
    <p>Provide accurate information needed for participation, keep account credentials private, and submit only work and files you are authorized to share. Do not impersonate another participant, access another person’s work, disrupt the service, or bypass contest restrictions. Contact organizers about access or accessibility difficulties before beginning a timed assessment.</p>
    <h2>Learning materials and attribution</h2>
    <p>Problems and solutions are available to read and download for study. Preserve the attribution and any license or reuse notice supplied with a resource. Free access does not by itself grant permission to republish materials, use sponsor logos, or claim authorship. Contact IMT about further reuse.</p>
    <h2>Submitted work</h2>
    <p>Submitting work allows organizers to store, review, and grade it for the competition. Participants remain responsible for the content they upload. Public results may name competitors and their placements, as in the existing archive. Questions about results or attribution should be raised with organizers.</p>
    <h2>Cost and refunds</h2>
    <p>IMT registration and competition materials are free. This website does not collect entry fees, so there is no entry-fee refund process.</p>
    <h2>External services and availability</h2>
    <p>Links to registration services, sponsors, and other resources may take you to independent websites with their own terms. Contact IMT promptly if an outage or technical problem affects your participation. Organizers will review contest issues under the event rules.</p>
    <h2>Privacy and younger participants</h2>
    <p>See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/cookies">cookies and storage notice</a>. A parent or guardian should contact IMT before a child under 13 uses features that collect information.</p>
    <h2>Contact and revisions</h2>
    <p>Contact <a href="mailto:info@integratedmath.org">info@integratedmath.org</a> with questions about these terms, resource permissions, or contest access. Revisions will be posted on this page.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
